# One repo, two checkouts: WSL and native Windows.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, which wants CRLF in the working
# tree. Neovim writes lazy-lock.json with LF, so every single nvim launch left
# the file showing as modified with an EMPTY content diff — noise that
# eventually gets committed by accident, and lazy-lock.json is precisely the
# file the two machines must agree on (update on one, `:Lazy restore` on the
# other).
#
# Pinning LF everywhere settles it. Nothing here needs CRLF: PowerShell reads
# LF scripts fine, and both windows/link.ps1 and windows/profile.ps1 are LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
